# ─── Dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# package-lock.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It pins every transitive
# dependency, so a teammate installing next month gets the versions this was
# tested against. Leaving it out is how an install silently drifts.

# ─── Machine-specific: never commit ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Real settings belong to whoever installed it; devcdp.settings.example.json is
# the one that ships.
devcdp.settings.json
devcdp.config.json
settings.json

# Learned memory and the session claim registry: local state, and memory entries
# can quote data from the app being debugged.
.devcdp/
*.jsonl

# Backups and temp files written by the setup wizard.
*.devcdp-backup-*
*.devcdp-tmp-*

# ─── Session materials ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The slide deck and handout still describe behaviour the tool no longer has
# (BACKLOG.md, DOC-4). Delete these two lines once they are reworded, if you want
# them distributed with the code.
DevCDP-session-slides.pdf
DevCDP-session-handout.pdf

# ─── Scratch work ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Throwaway scripts written while investigating. Keep this habit: put temporary
# files here or use these prefixes, and they can never be committed by accident.
scratch/
tmp/
probe-*.mjs
shoot-*.mjs
bench.*
*-audit.mjs
*-patch.mjs

# ─── Test and tooling output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
automation-output/
test-results/
coverage/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# ─── Screenshots and captures ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ignored by default because these are usually debugging leftovers, and a
# screenshot of a real app can contain customer data. Images that genuinely
# belong to the documentation are allowed through by the exceptions below.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.gif
!docs/**/*.png
!docs/**/*.gif
!extension/icons/*.png

# ─── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# ─── Editors and OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Note on generated files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# docs/TOOLS.md IS committed even though `npm run docs` generates it: the offline
# test suite regenerates it and fails if the committed copy differs, which is what
# stops the tool reference drifting from the tools.
